  rankdir="TB";
  "I_Init1" [label="(0,0,0) Deduction: Currently initiation is a pivot and σ recognizes elements, so specific interactions occur."];
  "I_Str1" [label="(0,0,0) Induction: In case PhoP shares similarity and comprises REC/DBD, it has conserved domains."];
  "NROOT" [label="(0,0,0) This study proposes to explain dual transcriptional control by Mycobacterium tuberculosis PhoP through structural and mechanistic analysis of PhoP-dependent activation complexes and a modeled repression complex, testing how PhoP dimers bind promoter PHO boxes, how PhoP may engage RNAP and affect σA–35 interactions during activation, and whether repression involves spacer-DNA distortion and interference with GlnR-associated activation.", fillcolor="lightyellow", style="filled"];
  "NROOT_COMMON" [label="(0,0,0) When a conserved bacterial response regulator has dual activator/repressor roles, binds defined promoter motifs, acts in the RNAP open-complex initiation pathway, and still has an inadequately understood mechanism, structural comparison of activation and repression assemblies is a scientifically appropriate way to test how DNA binding, RNAP engagement, σ-factor contacts, spacer-DNA geometry, and partner-factor interference may contribute to regulation."];
  "R11" [label="(0,0,0) Because PhoP regulates promoters containing multiple PHO boxes while the determinants of its differential dual regulation remain inadequately understood, the molecular details of PhoP promoter control require elucidation."];
  "R12" [label="(0,0,0) The unresolved mechanism by which PhoP differentially acts as a dual transcriptional regulator makes its promoter-recognition and regulatory mechanisms an open problem for structural and mechanistic study."];
  "R2" [label="(0,0,0) In σ-dependent bacterial transcription, specific promoter interactions provide the context in which transcription activators that recruit RNAP or bend DNA can facilitate RNAP-promoter open-complex formation."];
  "R4" [label="(0,0,0) Because transcription initiation is a critical step in bacterial gene expression, transcription repressors that use occlusion or locking mechanisms can inhibit initiation."];
  "R7" [label="(0,0,0) PhoP DNA binding involves both phosphorylation-enhanced affinity and recognition of specific direct-repeat PHO boxes."];
  "R9" [label="(0,0,0) A PhoP dimer contacts a PHO box through conserved winged helices, and these interactions are associated with a compact arrangement that restricts the 4-bp spacer between binding sites."];
  "S1" [label="(1,0,0) Transcription initiation is a critical pivot for gene expression in bacteria."];
  "S10" [label="(10,0,0) Commonly, a majority of OmpR/PhoB family response regulators function as dual functional transcription regulators."];
  "S14" [label="(14,0,0) Induction: In case many TFs are dual and commonly OmpR/PhoB are dual, so Mtb PhoP functions as global activator and repressor."];
  "S18" [label="(18,0,0) Known, what determines PhoP to differentially act as a dual transcriptional regulator remains inadequately understood."];
  "S19" [label="(19,0,0) Mtb PhoP shares high structural similarity with other homologous members."];
  "S2" [label="(2,0,0) Currently, the principal σ factor recognizes promoter consensus -10 and -35 elements."];
  "S20" [label="(20,0,0) Mtb PhoP comprises a conserved N-terminal receiver domain and a C-terminal DNA binding domain."];
  "S21" [label="(21,0,0) Phosphorylation of the REC enhances the DNA binding affinity of DBD."];
  "S22" [label="(22,0,0) PhoP binds to specific direct repeat units referred to as PHO boxes."];
  "S23" [label="(23,0,0) A PhoP dimer interacts with the PHO box through conserved winged helices."];
  "S24" [label="(24,0,0) Interactions facilitate a compact arrangement which restricts a 4-bp spacer between binding sites."];
  "S25" [label="(25,0,0) PhoP is capable of regulating multiple PHO promoters that consist of two or more PHO boxes."];
  "S4" [label="(4,0,0) If specific transcription activators recruit RNAP or bend DNA, then RPo formation is facilitated."];
  "S7" [label="(7,0,0) If transcription repressors utilize occlusion or locking, then transcription initiation is inhibited."];
  "S9" [label="(9,0,0) In case, many transcription factors have been identified as activators or repressors at different promoters."];
